{"seconds": 5.81354433298111, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-repairs-v1/submissions/A15/gpt-5-2025-08-07/format-r1.json", "submission_sha256": "1326b17124188e63641190fd6ab86082a84989b9667512e4529e7a825d1613cd", "code_sha256": "62d955a1c84acab3063aa5d4a7d50254c940c72b89cc358bccc8c8e582754782", "description": "Neuroscience A15 event detector: deterministic per-recording STFT feature extraction with 1 ms hop, 24 log-spaced triangular bands (250\u201312000 Hz), broadband log-energy, and 5/15 ms smoothed broadband features. Noise-floor normalization subtracts each recording\u2019s 20th-percentile log-energy (exact for validation/test, approximate via sparse sampling for non-validation training). A HistGradientBoostingClassifier is trained using up to 60k uniformly sampled frames. Threshold, gap-fill, and minimum-duration hyperparameters are selected by mean event F1 on a fixed validation subset of training recordings, using maximum-cardinality bipartite matching under the specified onset/offset tolerances. The classifier is then refit on all training recordings (re-using computed features where possible), and predictions are post-processed on test recordings to produce 1 ms binary rasters with zeros in padding. Deterministic seeds used; single-thread numeric workload; memory-conscious, streaming per recording.", "code_lines": 239, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

